{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Removed the `caused_by` -> fd4a-4e91-f179-4932 edge on closing not_a_bug.\n\n`metrics.bug_trends.caused_by_fan_in` counts caused_by links across ALL bugs with no\nclose_class filter, so leaving the edge in place would have counted a not_a_bug ticket as an\nescaped defect against that story and inflated its fan-in. The attribution was correct while\nthis was believed to be a defect; with that verdict reversed it is wrong data.\n\nThe evidence trail is unaffected — the introducing commit (8297083532a3, \"Add rebar-mcp HTTP\nservice to the AWS box\") is still named in the RCA above, so the origin is recoverable by\nreading rather than by a metric edge. If this ticket is ever reopened as a defect, restore the\nlink with: rebar link surreal-horsy-skimmer fd4a-4e91-f179-4932 caused_by"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787771888501664001,"uuid":"921d2f6d-6bb6-4598-b170-f78d5e9ed79c"}